@522. A confession and glorification by the Angels of Heaven, that the Lord is He who is, who lives and has power from Himself, and rules all things, because He alone is eternal and infinite. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@--. To "give thanks" = acknowledgement and glorification of the Lord. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@617. A celebration and glorification of the Lord before Him, and before the Angels of the higher Heavens. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@--[2]. "As it were a new song" = the celebration and glorification of the Lord in the New Christian Heaven... [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".] @618.

@665. "Who shall not... glorify Thy name" (Revelation 15:4) = that He alone is to be worshipped... To "glorify His name" = to worship Him. @AE 942. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@763. "In proportion as she has Glorified herself" (Revelation 18:7) = in the degree according to their elation of heart from dominion; for from this they glorify (praise) themselves. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@803. Preface. A glorification of the Lord by the Angels... that the Roman Catholic religiosity in the Spiritual World is removed. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@812. "Let us be glad and exult, and give glory to Him" = joy of soul and of heart, and the derivative glorification of the Lord... [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@--. To "give glory to Him" = to acknowledge, and confess that all truth is from the Lord; also to acknowledge that the Lord is the God of Heaven and earth; here, therefore, it = to glorify (praise) Him, because this involves both of these things.

@BE 32[end]. He uttered these words after His glorification, and His glorification was His full unition with His Father... and the Holy Spirit was the Divine proceeding from Him after His glorification.

@CL 3[6]. (The notion that the joy of Heaven consists in the perpetual glorification of God.) [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".] @9. @TCR 695.

@9[4]. By the glorification of God is meant to bring forth the fruits of love, that is, to do the work of our calling faithfully, sincerely, and with diligence... By this is God Glorified, and in this case by worship at stated times. Have you never read... "In this is My Father Glorified, that ye bring forth much fruit..." (John 15:8). You priests can be in the glorification of worship, because this is your office... [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@81. From the east to the west... was heard a glorification; and the Angel said to me, This glorification is a glorification of the Lord on account of His Advent... The glorifications and celebrations of the Lord are made from the Word. Illustrated. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".] @--[3].

@--[4]. There was (then) heard a general glorification from the east into the west of Heaven, and also from the south into the north. Illustrated. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".] @TCR 625.

@TCR 95. The passion... was not the act of redemption, but the act of the glorification of His Human.

@97[end]. This union is glorification.

@104. That the state of progression to union was His state of exinanition, and the union itself is the state of His glorification. The Lord... had two states, which are called those of exinanition and of glorification... The state of glorification is also the state of union; He was in this state when He was transfigured... and also when He did miracles...

@105. The reason He had these two states, of exinanition and of glorification. Explained.

@--. In a Word, the Lord glorified His Human, that is, made it Divine, in the same way as He regenerates man, that is, makes him spiritual. @684[end].

@110[4]. He asked the Father to glorify His name, that is, His Human. To "glorify" is to make Divine by union with Himself.

@117. Who divide the spoil, and then are glad and glorify (praise).

@126. That the passion... was the last temptation... and was the means of the glorification of His Human, that is, of union with the Divine of His Father; and was not redemption. General article.

@--. The glorification is the unition of the Lord with the Divine of His Father; this was done successively, and plenarily by the passion...

@128. Concerning the glorification, by which is meant the unition of the Lord's Divine Human with the Divine of the Father, and that it was fully completed by the passion... Illustrated. @AE 806[6]. @CanonsNC 20. Redeemer. 7. 5.

@139. The Divine and the Human, after the glorification, being united as the prior with its posterior, and as the essence with its form.

@599. The Lord... by combats... glorified His Human, that is, made it Divine; so with man... after temptation. He glorifies him, that is, renders him spiritual.

@SE 600. On a general glorification -glorificatione- in the Heavens. @604. a. @606. @3029. @4176.

@3029. Some in Hell wanted to glorify (praise) too.

@4845. (The glorification of the Lord's body.) Explained.

@DMin 4773. To glorify (praise) the Lord is not use, but recreation; for they glorify (praise) the Lord in every use...

@AE 33[2]. Thus and no otherwise is the Lord Glorified in man... "In this is My Father Glorified"...

@178. As the Lord when He glorified His Human (Signified); namely, that He dissipated all evils and falsities from the human He had from the mother.

@--. As He glorified His Human, so He regenerates man; that is, as He united His Divine to the Human and the Human to the Divine, so, with man, he conjoins the internal with the external and the external with the internal.

@183[10]. Because the Divine truth proceeds from the Lord's glorified Human, and not immediately from His Divine Itself, because this was glorified in Him from eternity. Signified.

@224[end]. To "glorify" (John 12) = to make Divine.

@228[2]. That (the Divine truth) will manifest the Lord's Divine Human, is signified by, "He shall glorify Me" (John 16:14). To "glorify" = to make the Lord's Divine Human known.

@288. Divine truth and Divine good, and glorification. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@--. "Thanksgiving" = glorification. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@--. Glorification, when from the Lord, = the perpetual influx of Divine good united to Divine truth with Angels and men; and, with these, the glorification of the Lord = reception, and acknowledgement at heart that all good and truth are from Him; and thence all intelligence, wisdom, and happiness. Moreover, all the glorification of the Lord which is performed by Angels and men is not from themselves, but Hows in from Him. The glorification which is from men and not from the Lord is not from the heart, but only from what is active in the memory... and is not heard in Heaven... This glorification is not acknowledgement at heart that all good and truth are from the Lord... Love is life according to the Lord's precepts. When man is in this life, there is the glorification of the Lord... from the heart; which is meant by to be "Glorified" in John 15:8. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@--[10]. His state of humiliation is described by...; and His state of glorification by, "Thou hast crowned him with glory and honour" (Psalms 8:5).

@321. As this celebration and glorification is a living acknowledgement that the Lord's Human is Divine, and that He has omnipotence and omniscience... [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@328[20]. He continually delivers by His having glorified His Human... @806[2].

@340. Acknowledgement and glorification of the Lord on this account. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@--[5]. To "bless Jehovah" = to glorify (praise) Him... and as all glorification of Him is from spiritual truths and from spiritual good, it is said... To "sing a song" = to glorify (praise) from these truths and this good. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@476[end]. No Angel is allowed to think of the Lord's passion, but of His glorification...

@518[20]. The glorification of the Lord by the universal Heaven. Signified. (in Psalms 98) The glorification by its ultimates is signified by... The glorification by the whole Heaven is signified by... The glorification of the Lord through the truths of intelligence and the goods of love is signified by... [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@581[12]. It is said the Lord's Divine Sensuous, because the Lord... glorified, that is, made Divine, His whole Human, even to its ultimate; (for) He left nothing in the sepulchre... The ultimate Sensuous, which the Lord glorified, is signified by the brazen serpent... The brazen serpent = ... the Lord's glorified or Divine Sensuous.

@619[15]. The Lord disclosed to His disciples that He had glorified... His whole human, even as to the Natural and Sensuous thereof. Signified. (by His showing His hands and feet, and by eating before them).

@655[10]. "The third day He shall rise again" = the plenary glorification of the Lord's Human.

@659[19]. "Burial"... with respect to the Lord, = the glorification of His Human; for the Lord glorified His whole Human... and therefore rose again on the third day with the Human glorified or made Divine... The resurrection of man to life is solely from... the union of His Divine with His Human, which is properly meant by glorification... @706[6].

@748. The Human glorified is the Divine Human.

@854. The glorification of the Lord from Divine truths. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@855. The glorification of the Lord from His Celestial Kingdom. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@856. The glorification of the Lord from His Spiritual Kingdom. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@900[2]. "He shall see, shall be satisfied" = glorification.

@935. The glorification of the Lord from spiritual affection. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@942. Good fears the Lord, and truths glorify (praise) Him.

@943. "And shall glorify Thy name" (Revelation 15:4) = the worship of the Lord from the truths derived from that good. [Here, glorify is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@1118. To "glorify herself" = to acquire glory for themselves. [Here, glorify is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@1197. "Alleluia" = the glorification of the Lord... "Alleluia" means "Praise ye God", thus, "Glorify ye the Lord." [Here, glorify is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@1214. The glorification of the Lord by all in the Heavens, on account of the rejection of the evil, and the consequent deliverance of the good. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@1215. The glorification of Him from truths. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@1216. The glorification of Him from the goods of love. Signified. [Here, glorification is being used in the sense of its meaning "praise".]

@Ath 161. The Lord... rising from the sepulchre glorified Himself. Signified.

@162. Thus the Lord, thoroughly and clearly glorified, rose with the Human.

@LJPost 87. Therefore He could glorify the whole body, so that as to that body which is rejected and putrefies with those who are born of human parents, it was with Him glorified and made Divine from the Divine in Him; and with this He rose again...

@DeVerbo 14[5]. In the celestial Word... in the first chapter (of Genesis) is described the glorification of the Lord's Human. Explained.

@CanonsNC 19. Redeemer. 6. 2. That the state of glorification was a state of unition with the Father.

@CanonsNC 21. Redeemer. 8. After the completed unition, He returned into the Divine in which He was from eternity, together with and in the glorified Human.

@CanonsNC 30. Redemption. 7. 6. Thus successively glorified His Human.

