@DP 216. When he sees the evil in glory...

@217[5]. A person who is in dignity there, is indeed in magnificence and glory...

@249. All gloryings over impieties are permissions...

@252[2]. In wars... from the love of glory he is in the delight of killing... To do this for the sake of one's own glory is diabolical...

@324[2]. As the Divine is of glory inexhaustible...

@AR 22. To "Him be glory and strength..." (Revelation 1:6) = to Whom alone is Divine majesty and omnipotence... By "glory," in the Word, where the Lord is treated of, is meant the Divine majesty, and it is predicated of His Divine wisdom.

@24. By "the glory" in which they will see Him (Matthew 24:30) is meant the Word in the spiritual sense.

@249. "The animals gave glory, and honour, and thanksgiving to Him..." (Revelation 4:9) = that the Word ascribes all truth, good, and worship to the Lord... For His "glory" is from Divine truth; and His "honour," from Divine good. Illustrated. @253. @288. @291. @804.

@517. "They gave glory to the God of Heaven" (Revelation 11:13) = that they acknowledged the Lord, and were separated... To "give glory" = to acknowledge and worship. @AE 678.

@629. "Give glory to Him..." (Revelation 14:7) = acknowledgement and confession that all the truth of the Word is from the Lord... ( = to live according to Divine truth. @AE 874.)

@--. By "glory" the Angels perceive nothing but Divine truth; and as all Divine truth is from the Lord, by to "give glory to Him" they perceive to acknowledge and confess that all truth is from Him; for all the glory in the Heavens is from no other source; and in proportion as a Society... is in Divine truth... the Angels are in the resplendence of glory.

@--[2]. That by "glory" is meant Divine truth. Illustrated.

@674. "The temple was filled with smoke from the glory of God and from His power" (Revelation 15:8) = the inmost of Heaven full of Divine spiritual and celestial truth from the Lord... By "glory" is signified Divine spiritual truth. (Compare @AE 955.)

@693. "Not to give Him glory" (Revelation 16:9) = not to receive in faith that the Lord is the God of Heaven and earth.

@812. Under <Glorify>, see this reference.

@897. "Having the glory of God" (Revelation 21:11) = that in that Church the Word will be understood... By "the glory of God" is signified the Word in its Divine light. Illustrated.

@919. "For the glory of God did enlighten it" (Revelation 21:23) = that the men of that Church... will be in spiritual light from the Divine truth of the Word... "The glory of God" = the Divine truth of the Word.

@921. To "bring glory and honour into it" (Revelation 21:23) = to confess the Lord, and ascribe to Him all the truth and good which they have; (for) "glory" is predicated of Divine truth. @923.

@940. That the men in the New Jerusalem will not be in Knowledges from... glory originating in pride. Signified.

@--[2]. There is a natural lumen from glory which originates in pride, and also not from pride. Explained.

@CL 7[4]. (The honour and glory of the governors in Heaven.)

@13[end]. They who are in the love of glory, not from use, do not receive this influx.

@208[2]. Yon glory over us... but we do not glory over you...

@263[4]. (The devil said) We glory to eternity... we are allowed to glory... @264[3].

@269[6]. Devils have rationality from the glory of the love of self; for the love of self is encompassed with glory; and glory elevates the understanding even into the light of Heaven.

